{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773308812,"nonce":"lzxCcpEohxJFkW6bmT+fYklVzeU=","title":"Watcher stops when backgrounded: docker -it flag reads stdin","message":"When running `nightshift watcher \u0026`, the process periodically stops (SIGTTIN) because Docker containers are launched with `-it` flags.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`host/docker_cmd.py:42`:\n```python\ntty_flags = [\"-it\"] if sys.stdin.isatty() else []\n```\n\nWhen the watcher is backgrounded with `\u0026`, it still has a TTY attached. Docker `-it` tries to allocate a pseudo-TTY and connect stdin, which triggers SIGTTIN when the background process attempts stdin access.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe `-it` flag should only be used for interactive CLI sessions (e.g. `nightshift start` run directly by a user). When launched by the watcher or any non-interactive context, containers should run without `-it`.\n\nOptions:\n1. Pass a `interactive=False` parameter from the watcher to `build_docker_cmd()` and skip `-it`\n2. Never use `-it` since containers are fire-and-forget (`-p` mode) and never read stdin\n\nOption 2 is simpler and correct — nightshift containers never need interactive stdin.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `nightshift watcher \u0026` does not stop with SIGTTIN\n- [ ] Containers launched by watcher never use `-it`\n- [ ] `nightshift start` still works correctly (with or without `-it`)\n\nREQ-001","files":null}]}